/A 2741 0 R
/Alt (The six-panel flowchart arranged in a single vertical column illustrates a multi-hazard risk assessment process. Panel 1, labeled Data Acquisition, shows a database icon with a download arrow and lists Satellite, Meteorological, Socio-economic, Environmental and Vector Datasets. A downward arrow points to Panel 2, labeled GIS Processing and Criteria Preparation, which shows three stacked map layers and describes data preprocessing including projection, clipping, resampling, reclassification, and selection of indicators. A downward arrow points to Panel 3, which contains three horizontally connected circles: Hazard Indicators \(11\) with a house icon, Vulnerability Indicators \(17\) with a people icon, and Mitigation Capacity Indicators \(6\) with a shield and checkmark icon. A downward arrow points to Panel 4, labeled Standardization and AHP Weighting, showing a balance scale icon and describing normalization \(0 to 1\), AHP weighting, and consistency test \(CR less than 0.10\). A downward arrow points to Panel 5, labeled Multi-Hazard Risk Assessment, which displays a 5x5 grid of squares transitioning from green to red, and includes the formula Risk equals \(H times V\) slash M.)
