/A 2744 0 R
/Alt (The two-panel map shows a regional view of Bangladesh on the right and a detailed map of the Kalapara Coastal Area, Kuakata, on the left. The right panel displays a map with horizontal axis labels from 90 degrees 0 minutes 0 seconds E to 90 degrees 40 minutes 0 seconds E and vertical axis labels from 21 degrees 40 minutes 0 seconds N to 22 degrees 20 minutes 0 seconds N. It features dark green landmasses, a light green study area, and a dark blue Bay of Bengal. Geographic labels include Pirojpur, Jhalokati, Bagerhat, Barguna, Patuakhali, and Bhola. An inset map in the upper right shows India and Bangladesh with a red rectangle indicating the regional map location. A black arrow points from the light green study area in the right panel to the left panel. The left panel, titled &#x00022;Kalapara Coastal Area, Kuakata&#x00022;, shows a detailed map with horizontal axis labels from 90 degrees 4 minutes 48 seconds E to 90 degrees 18 minutes 52 seconds E and vertical axis labels from 21 degrees 49 minutes 48 seconds N to 22 degrees 3 minutes 52 seconds N. It depicts an irregularly shaped landmass outlined in red, representing Kalapara, Kuakata, with numerous light blue river channels and dotted patterns indicating settlements. A north arrow and a scale bar from 0 to 24 miles are present.)
