800 0 obj
<<
/A 2853 0 R
/Alt (The six-panel map series arranged in two rows of three shows spatial distributions for six different criteria across a geographical area. Each panel includes a vertical gradient legend from 0 darker region to 1 brighter region and white lines representing water bodies. Panel A, HAND, shows predominantly brighter regions high values across most of the map, with sparse darker regions. Panel B, Clay Content, displays mixed values, with intermediate values widespread and brighter regions at the upper and lower extremities. Panel C, Water pH, is dominated by brighter regions high values throughout the area. Panel D, Soil pH, presents a mixed distribution similar to Panel B, with intermediate values widespread and brighter regions at the upper and lower extremities. Panel E, Salinity Level, exhibits a clear gradient with the brightest regions highest values centrally located, decreasing outwards to darker regions at the periphery. Panel F, Sand Dragging, is mostly darker regions low values, with localized brighter regions high values forming concentric patterns in the upper right and central right areas. A compass rose pointing North and a horizontal scale bar labeled Miles with ticks at 0, 7, and 14 are at the bottom right.)
/K 14
/P 44 0 R
/Pg 19 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
