1382 0 obj
<<
/A 2975 0 R
/Alt (The six-panel map series, arranged in two rows of three, displays spatial distribution of social vulnerability criteria across a geographic region. Each panel presents a map of the same landmass, divided into irregular sub-regions, with a vertical legend showing a brightness gradient from 0 to 1. A compass rose with a north arrow and a scale bar marked 0, 7, 14 miles are at the bottom right. Panel A, titled Population Density, shows higher density darker regions in the upper central and lower central parts of the landmass. Panel B, titled Literacy Rate, displays higher literacy rates darker regions in the far right and lower central parts. Panel C, titled Population Hotspot, presents a speckled pattern, with denser, darker speckles hotspots concentrated in the upper central and lower central areas. Panel D, titled Female Population, indicates higher female population darker regions in the upper central, far right, and lower central areas. Panel E, titled Dependent population, shows higher dependent population darker regions in the upper central and lower central areas. Panel F, titled Dependent Agriculture, displays higher dependent agriculture darker regions in the upper central, far right, and lower central areas.)
/K 14
/P 44 0 R
/Pg 23 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
