/A 3004 0 R
/Alt (The five-panel map series shows the spatial distribution of five indicators across an irregular landmass, with white lines indicating internal boundaries. A legend to the right of Panel E displays normalized values, ranging from High-1 \(red\) to Low-1 \(green\). A scale bar below the legend indicates distances in miles, with tick marks at 0, 7, and 14 miles, and a north arrow. Panel A, labeled Settlement Density, shows two prominent areas of high density \(brighter red\) in the upper central and lower left regions, with density decreasing to low \(green\) in surrounding areas. Panel B, labeled NDVI, displays a varied distribution, with higher values \(darker green\) along some outer edges and internal areas, and lower values \(yellow and red\) scattered throughout. Panel C, labeled Distance to Settlement, is predominantly high \(red\), indicating most areas are far from settlements, with some lower values \(yellow and green\) near settlement locations. Panel D, labeled Coastal Vegetation, shows very low values \(red\) across most of the landmass, with only small patches of higher values \(darker green\) indicating coastal vegetation along some edges. Panel E, labeled LULC, presents a complex mosaic of values, with green areas prominent in the lower left and upper right, yellow areas widespread, and red areas scattered, reflecting diverse land use and land cover types.)
/K 133
/P 44 0 R
/Pg 24 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
