/A 3018 0 R
/Alt (The four-panel map series, arranged in two rows of two, displays spatial distribution of various proximity and distance indicators across a landmass. Each panel includes a vertical legend bar showing a gradient from darker green at 0 to brighter red at 1. Panel A, titled Cyclone Center Proximity, shows numerous small, concentric circular patterns of brighter red, yellow-green, and darker green distributed across the landmass, indicating many points of high proximity. Panel B, titled Road Distance, displays a dense network of brighter red lines and surrounding yellow-green and darker green bands, representing roads and their proximity. Panel C, titled Health Center Proximity, presents several larger, concentric circular patterns of brighter red, yellow-green, and darker green, indicating fewer points of high proximity compared to Panel A. Panel D, titled Distance to Coastal Forest, shows brighter red areas concentrated along the coastal edges of the landmass, transitioning to yellow-green and then predominantly darker green towards the interior. Panel D also includes a compass rose labeled N and a scale bar with values 0, 7, and 14 Miles. White lines represent water bodies or rivers across all maps.)
