/A 3043 0 R
/Alt (The two-panel map displays spatial hazard distribution. Panel A, arranged in two rows of two, shows individual hazard components. Panel A sub-panel \(a\) Cyclone Hazard map shows central and southern landmass areas with High to Very High hazard. Panel A sub-panel \(b\) Flood Hazard map shows similar central and southern landmass areas with High to Very High hazard. Panel A sub-panel \(c\) Salinity Hazard map indicates High to Very High hazard along the river and southern regions. Panel A sub-panel \(d\) Erosion Hazard map shows High to Very High hazard along the river and southern coastal regions. A common legend for Panel A defines Very Low, Low, Moderate, High, and Very High hazard levels. Panel B, to the right of Panel A, presents an Integrated Hazard map, showing widespread Moderate, High, and Very High hazard across most of the landmass, with central and southern areas predominantly High to Very High. Both panels include a north arrow and a scale bar marked 0, 7, 14 Miles.)
