/Alt (The three-panel map arranged in two rows shows vulnerability assessments. Panel A, labeled Physical Vulnerability, displays a landmass with intricate water channels. The landmass is primarily light green to yellow, indicating low to moderate vulnerability, with scattered orange to red regions of high to very high vulnerability, especially in central and southern areas. Panel B, labeled Social Vulnerability, shows the same landmass with larger, contiguous regions. High to very high vulnerability orange to red is prominent in the northern and southern parts, while the central area is mostly low to moderate light green to yellow. Panel C, labeled Integrated Vulnerability, presents the landmass with widespread high to very high vulnerability orange to red across central and southern regions, with fewer low to moderate areas compared to Panel A. A legend below Panel B and to the right of Panel C defines Vulnerability Rank: darker green for Very Low, lighter green for Low, yellow for Moderate, orange for High, and red for Very High. A north arrow and a scale bar marked 0, 7, 14 Miles are also present.)
/K 5
/P 44 0 R
/Pg 30 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
