/A 3074 0 R
/Alt (The line graph titled &#x00022;Multi Hazard Risk Validation&#x00022; plots True Positive Rate on the vertical axis against False Positive Rate on the horizontal axis, both ranging from 0.0 to 1.0. Three lines are displayed. A solid blue line, labeled &#x00022;Risk Model Accuracy equals 0.91&#x00022;, starts at 0.0, 0.0 and shows a step-wise increase, rising vertically then moving horizontally, staying above the diagonal &#x00022;Random Guess&#x00022; line. It reaches 0.0, 0.45, then 0.05, 0.45, then 0.05, 0.65, then 0.1, 0.65, then 0.1, 0.8, then 0.25, 0.8, then 0.25, 0.95, then 0.35, 0.95, and finally extends to 1.0, 1.0. A dashed black line, labeled &#x00022;Random Guess&#x00022;, extends diagonally from 0.0, 0.0 to 1.0, 1.0. A dashed blue line, labeled &#x00022;Perfect Line&#x00022;, starts at 0.0, 0.0, rises vertically to 0.0, 1.0, and then extends horizontally to 1.0, 1.0. The legend is in the bottom right.)
